            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This is interesting, but I think other platforms also do sled-cycles (or something equivalent).  I wonder if there is a way for us to make this more common.\n\nShould we supply a script with the `phosphor-static-norootfs-init` package that can will remount /mnt/persist as RO and then that can be called for multiple machines?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Robert Ercean Dima",
                        "email": "robert3@meta.com",
                        "username": "robert-ercean"
                    },
                    "message": "@patrick@stwcx.xyz\n\nI think that would imply making the phosphor-static-norootfs-init/init script also skip the newly added file(besides just \"init\"), right?\nBecause it currently iterates through all files inside /usr/libexec/phosphor-static-norootfs-init/:\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/blob/master/meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/initrdscripts/phosphor-static-norootfs-init/init"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Robert Ercean Dima",
                        "email": "robert3@meta.com",
                        "username": "robert-ercean"
                    },
                    "message": "Or should this logic remain in meta-facebook/recipes-phosphor ?"
                }
            ],
